## Stack
- Backend: Spring Boot 4, Java 21, Maven wrapper; Oracle (Dev onwards), H2/embedded Postgres locally; Kafka
- Frontend: Angular (strict TypeScript, standalone components)
- Delivery: GitLab CI → OpenShift GitOps (Argo CD), Helm, HashiCorp Vault

## Where things live
- Specs, one folder per feature: `docs/specs/<feature>/` (see `docs/specs/README.md`)
- Decisions: `docs/memory/decisions.md`, ADRs in `docs/adr/`
- Known pitfalls: `docs/memory/gotchas.md`; terms: `docs/memory/glossary.md`
- Quality gate thresholds: `eco.gates.yaml`

## Non-negotiable rules
1. Every change traces to a requirement ID (`REQ-nnn`) and has tests; write the test first.
2. Never put real personal data (PII) in prompts, code, tests, fixtures or logs. Use synthetic data.
3. Never read or print secrets (.env, keys, Vault tokens, kube or AWS credentials).
4. Never deploy, run `oc`/`kubectl` against anything except Dev, or force-push.
5. A task is done only when the gates in `eco.gates.yaml` pass. Report failures honestly.
